# Platform JS edits (`index.html` + `cch-*.js`)

## Before every deploy

1. **Bump cache buster** on every changed `<script src="cch-*.js?v=...">` in `platform/index.html`. Browsers cache JS aggressively; unchanged `?v=` = stale code live.
2. **Syntax check** each touched JS file:

```powershell
cd C:\dev\CCH-Platform-Deploy\cch-deploy
```

```powershell
node --check platform\cch-your-file.js
```

3. **Verify file tail** after edits to large CRLF files (`index.html`, `cch-proposals-invoices-fix.js`, etc.). Blind writes have truncated files twice — read last ~20 lines; file must end with valid closing braces/tags.

## Cache buster convention

- Per-feature tags: `poc11`, `om25`, `20260628ds3`, etc.
- Bump **every** script tag whose source file you changed, not just one.
- After deploy, confirm live URL serves new query string (View Source or Network tab).

## `index.html` rules

- **Do not split** — single-file architecture is intentional (~32K lines).
- Use exact-string Edit/replace; do not write Node patch scripts for routine edits.
- `CCH_BUILD` near line ~3452 is the sidebar build tag — bump when shipping a user-visible release batch.

## Post-edit smoke (staging)

```powershell
firebase deploy --only hosting:platform --project staging
```

Hard refresh staging → login → navigate to the page you changed → confirm no console syntax errors.
